# What a change reaches that the Go import graph can't show, for
# scripts/integ-select.py. A line is a path (a file, or a directory ending in
# /) and the test files that change reaches; # starts a comment.
#
# Most of the mapping needs no line here: the selector follows Go imports and
# init-time registrations from each test file, and a test file that reads a
# repo file by a "../../<path>" literal is chosen when that path changes. A
# line is for what neither shows, such as a file the harness reads for a test.

